meta { title = "Kalandra 0.99.4 — cooperative GPU kernels, streams, networking and C interop", description = "Workgroup GPU kernels, GPU UTF-8 text, combined CUDA+Vulkan bundles, streams, subprocesses, directory watching, TCP networking and C interop.", order = 0, group = "Release archive" }

Kalandra 0.99.4 expands GPU programming and host systems support: cooperative workgroup GPU kernels in std/gpu, UTF-8 text processing on GPUs, combined CUDA and Vulkan application bundles and release compiler packages, byte streams and OS subprocesses, recursive filesystem operations and directory watching, event-driven TCP networking, C/C++ header imports and library exports, and -O0 through -O3 optimization controls. This page covers changes since 0.99.3.

Existing 0.99.3 programs require no syntax migration. The compiler and native language server report 0.99.4; the separately versioned VS Code extension is 0.3.0.

