h2 { "Native C/C++ interop, CLI and editor tools" }

Kalandra modules can import declarations directly from C headers using the destination ABI, pass checked noescape callbacks or handle-managed subscriptions (acquire_handle, release_handle and use_handle), enforce main-thread APIs marked with @MainActor, and exchange fixed-width C structs and counted UTF-8 text. Use export "C" fn or export "C" direct fn with kalandra --emit static, shared or object and --header to produce C/C++-callable libraries and matching headers. The cross-platform window example in native/examples/window opens a resizable GUI window on AppKit, Win32 and X11 from one Kalandra program.

The compiler now accepts -O0, -O1, -O2 and -O3 while preserving checked arithmetic, floating-point policy, ownership and cancellation. Pairing --no-link with --emit-mlir or --emit-llvm validates frontend checking, MLIR lowering and LLVM IR emission without producing an object file or invoking the host linker. kalandra remove deletes a direct manifest dependency and prunes unreachable lock entries offline. Interactive terminal builds display phase timings, with --silent and --debug flags for scripts and logs.

The 0.3.0 VS Code extension and 0.99.4 native language server add export "C" direct highlighting, std/net import-path completion, and crash-free trait conformance checking when an unrelated function signature in the workspace has diagnostics.

